# Story 60: Web Fetch (40s)
# Hook: Point the agent at a URL -- web_fetch pulls the page and summarizes it for you.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-060-web-fetch.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Point the agent at a URL -- web_fetch pulls the page and summarizes it for you.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
Double-press Escape for prompt mode.

[00:13.0 --> 00:32.0]
Give it a link and ask for a summary. The web_fetch tool pulls the URL's content and hands it to the agent, which reads it and distills the page into a few lines. Fetching is read-only -- no approval prompt.

[00:32.0 --> 00:37.0]
Pair web_fetch with web_search and the agent can find a source, open it, and bring the relevant details back into your terminal -- all from one prompt.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Any page on the web, summarized in your pane.

